// txtprt -- TXTPRT (S011560), print the words of list IO with one blank
// between, in lines of at most ROOM characters, broken at the last blank; a
// word longer than a line is cut at the line's end. Every line ends with
// newline. A reply's numbers and sublists do not print.
// txtAll does the same for CHANGE, where every item of list IO prints, a
// number as its six characters (unpack), a sublist as ( and ) around its
// items. txtRun is as txtAll, from reader IO, the items up to the next
// sublist of that list, or its end. txtOne is as txtAll, from reader IO, the
// next item only.
